  "slug": "arabidopsis-mediated-f99c",
  "summary": "Recent studies map hormone-regulatory nodes to specific promoters, splice events and microRNA targets across Brassica, cotton and Arabidopsis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is transcriptional and post-transcriptional control of hormone pathways. Several items target ABA: GhNAC029 represses GhNCED1 to reduce ABA synthesis and drought tolerance in cotton, methylation of the BraCYP707A3.A02 promoter blocks BraBPC2.A08 binding to regulate ABA catabolism and clubroot resistance in Brassica, and SRPKII-mediated splicing of HAB1 shapes ABA sensitivity during Arabidopsis seedling establishment. ANAC030 promotes leaf senescence by coupling JA biosynthesis to programmed cell death and chlorophyll metabolism. The miR159a-BrMYB12 module links a myo-inositol and raffinose axis to heat tolerance in flowering Chinese cabbage. The maize H2A.Z study addresses chromatin distribution across leaf and endosperm rather than hormone signaling and is therefore peripheral to this thread. What is new is the explicit mapping of hormone-regulatory nodes to specific promoters, splice events and microRNA targets.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
